item.description:
The fallacy of national cliches It happens in almost every international workshop I attend. Somewhere between the morning coffee and the first breakout session, someone drops a familiar cultural cliché with a knowing smile: &ldquo;Well, you know how Italians are with schedules,&rdquo; &ldquo;Germans are always punctual,&rdquo; or &ldquo;Of course the French wants wine at dinner.&rdquo;
Everyone chuckles and nods. Meanwhile, I feel an immediate spike of frustration.
It isn’t just that these remarks feel lazy or mildly awkward.
